{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Gerrymap you practice <strong>gerrymandering</strong>: drawing maps to decide the outcome of elections.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A state has four districts. In most elections, its vote is split equally. Each party should have two districts, right?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=289 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >NO! If we control redistricting, we pack the enemy party into just one district! This is the art of gerrymandering.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=286 /></span>It's not always so simple. A &quot;dummymander&quot; could give away all your seats in a bad election year. An overly conservative map could make further gains difficult. Also, some areas are very elastic, others are not!       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=298 /></span>The VRA says you have to create majority-minority districts in some states. As you play on the Democratic side in the campaign, this will force you to pack your voters! And expect to draw a lot of <strong>squiggly lines</strong>.       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Featuring</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A campaign mode with 10 states!</strong> Deal with the challenges Southern Democrats faced gerrymandering in 1990.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A sandbox mode with all 48 contiguous US states!</strong>\u00a01976-2000 Presidential, Senate and Gubernatorial results for each state. Play around with it!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1990 census data:\u00a0</strong>Race,\u00a0sex,\u00a0age,\u00a0household\u00a0income,\u00a0and\u00a0educational\u00a0attainment! </p></li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4120690?t=1768402529","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/279f161d45c5062425bb77b8e02a004d0c6dc506/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1768402529","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/e33e9da194e2f257f6bf34f5e8f1499e14589450/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1768402529","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/e33e9da194e2f257f6bf34f5e8f1499e14589450/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1768402529","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Camera Comfort","id":67},{"description":"Mouse Only Option","id":76},{"description":"Playable without Timed Input","id":74},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"demos":[{"appid":4187690,"description":""}],"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >In Gerrymap you practice <strong>gerrymandering</strong>: drawing maps to decide the outcome of elections.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A state has four districts. In most elections, its vote is split equally. Each party should have two districts, right?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/ef1c4595ed2e0e214fbdd3edf58c0393.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=289 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >NO! If we control redistricting, we pack the enemy party into just one district! This is the art of gerrymandering.\u00a0</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/eeb66092f0a327cfcadb15460b9a8bb0.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=286 /></span>It's not always so simple. A &quot;dummymander&quot; could give away all your seats in a bad election year. An overly conservative map could make further gains difficult. Also, some areas are very elastic, others are not!       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.avif?t=1768402529\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/extras_big/7ef1950baac4c5d60a7a2ce654706d91.webp?t=1768402529 width=1560 height=298 /></span>The VRA says you have to create majority-minority districts in some states. As you play on the Democratic side in the campaign, this will force you to pack your voters! And expect to draw a lot of <strong>squiggly lines</strong>.       </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Featuring</strong>:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A campaign mode with 10 states!</strong> Deal with the challenges Southern Democrats faced gerrymandering in 1990.</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A sandbox mode with all 48 contiguous US states!</strong>\u00a01976-2000 Presidential, Senate and Gubernatorial results for each state. Play around with it!</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1990 census data:\u00a0</strong>Race,\u00a0sex,\u00a0age,\u00a0household\u00a0income,\u00a0and\u00a0educational\u00a0attainment! </p></li></ul>","developers":["Gideon Kennedy"],"genres":[{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4120690/7378096fb6e62842c1620ace192fe4adb582a052/header.jpg?t=1768402529","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/4120690/786746701/7df1052457f0320c29947cf98d9c4f9c9d7ab738/1763255055/dash_av1.mpd?t=1763256202","dash_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/4120690/786746701/7df1052457f0320c29947cf98d9c4f9c9d7ab738/1763255055/dash_h264.mpd?t=1763256202","highlight":true,"hls_h264":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/4120690/786746701/7df1052457f0320c29947cf98d9c4f9c9d7ab738/1763255055/hls_264_master.m3u8?t=1763256202","id":257232378,"name":"Gerrymap Trailer","thumbnail":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/257232378/6ad20cda073be7ba62a1ed11405159afaa84e128/movie_600x337.jpg?t=1763256202"}],"name":"Gerrymap","package_groups":[{"description":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","name":"default","save_text":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","subs":[{"can_get_free_license":"0","is_free_license":false,"option_description":"","option_text":"Gerrymap - $9.99 USD","pa